From: zeitwaage interop harness
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the stratum-1 leap indicator across time snapshot updates

NtpManager::new marks a local-stratum=1 server as synchronized by setting
time_snapshot.leap_indicator, but the daemon's timer loop calls
update_time_snapshot() unconditionally and assigns the whole struct, so that
value is discarded on the first tick. With no sources the controller never
produces a leap indicator of its own, leaving the server advertising
flags.synchronized together with leap=Unknown - which conforming clients
(chrony, ntp5-exp) correctly refuse.

Re-assert the stratum-1 value after the assignment.

---
--- a/ntp-proto/src/system.rs
+++ b/ntp-proto/src/system.rs
@@ -275,6 +275,12 @@
     }

     pub fn update_time_snapshot(&self, time_snapshot: TimeSnapshot) {
-        self.server_info.write().unwrap().time_snapshot = time_snapshot;
+        let mut server_info = self.server_info.write().unwrap();
+        server_info.time_snapshot = time_snapshot;
+        // A stratum 1 server has no sources, so the controller never yields a
+        // leap indicator and the value set in new() would be lost here.
+        if self.synchronization_config.local_stratum == 1 {
+            server_info.time_snapshot.leap_indicator = NtpLeapIndicator::NoWarning;
+        }
     }
 }
